        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): keep DM topic auto-rename user message UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "<!--\nAI-assisted: generated with Cursor / Claude Sonnet 4.6\n-->\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users who send long Telegram messages containing emoji as their first turn in a DM topic session would get a garbled or empty auto-renamed topic title.\n\nOpenClaw can automatically rename Telegram forum topics on the first turn of a session. To do this it truncates the user's message to 500 characters and passes it to an LLM for label generation. The truncation uses `.slice(0, 500)`, which counts UTF-16 code units. Emoji and other characters outside the Basic Multilingual Plane are represented as surrogate pairs (two UTF-16 code units). If such a character straddles the 500-unit boundary, the slice discards the second half of the pair, producing an isolated high surrogate — invalid Unicode.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace `.slice(0, 500)` with `truncateUtf16Safe(..., 500)`, which backs up one code unit when the cut point falls inside a surrogate pair. This helper is the established pattern for all user-text truncation in the codebase (`openclaw/plugin-sdk/text-utility-runtime`).\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers sending emoji-heavy first messages in Telegram DM topic sessions (e.g. `\"Hi 👋 tell me about 🦞🦞🦞 …\"` long enough to reach 500 chars) would receive a malformed auto-topic label — either a replacement character, garbled output, or a rejected model call. After this fix the topic label is always derived from a valid Unicode string.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Affected path:** `extensions/telegram/src/bot-message-dispatch.ts` lines 3077–3094: `userMessage` is built by `.slice(0, 500)` then passed directly to `generateTopicLabel({ userMessage, … })`, which calls the LLM.\n- **Fix:** `truncateUtf16Safe(ctxPayload.RawBody ?? ctxPayload.Body ?? \"\", 500)` — same semantics, surrogate-safe boundary.\n- **Pattern match:** `truncateUtf16Safe` is used in the same way throughout the Telegram plugin for other string limits (e.g. thread name caps) and was added for exactly this class of bug.\n- **Diff:** 2-line change — one new import, one call-site replacement; no logic change.\n\n- [x] AI-assisted (Cursor / Claude Sonnet 4.6)\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns\n",
